Add a TESTNET-only admin RPC that disconnects active peers by IP address.

This is derived from xahaud commit 6fc14f398d754283b5dee6576edb59dc2656eaaa,
with port parsing and matching removed for distinct-IP local testnets.

This patch is intentionally manual and is not applied by xr-build. It targets
the compatible xahaud source shape before the commit above added its port-aware
handler. Run `git apply --check` before `git apply`; a tree already containing
that handler should fail the check.

The RPC is registered as admin but has no compile-time TESTNET guard. Keep the
admin endpoint local. One request stops every active peer sharing the supplied
IP, so do not use this IP-only variant as a public/NAT gateway control.

